## Session 42 summary

Working criterion #19, `posix_semantics_multi16` (the gate's last FAIL). Two root causes down this session:

**Fix 1 — shortform-dir readdir coherency (build `56453207`, VERIFIED).** Implemented sess41's design: `MXFS_IF_DIR_RELOAD` flag armed by the evict-ring DIR_MODIFY callback for LOCAL-format dirs, consumed in `xfs_readdir` via an event-driven `mxfs_dlm_reload_inode` before shortform getdents. Standalone `test_concurrent_touch` went 5/5 PASS with all 16 nodes converging in 50-54s, zero barrier timeouts; `cross_visibility` and `dir_stress` also clean.

**Fix 2 — P34D FUA-vs-SCST-cache lost update (build `863173A4`, built, NOT yet verified).** Fix 1 exposed the real remaining blocker: in-suite, almost every test's first barrier durably loses exactly one node's signal (touch succeeds, own readdir shows it, then it vanishes everywhere forever → every node burns the full 120s barrier timeout → suite blows 600s). Instrumented barrier_signal/barrier_wait proved it's not an mkdir-incarnation race; the victim's dmesg showed `P91-RELOAD-PROTECT`+`P34D-RELOAD-FRESHSRC` firing 13×. Root: with `fua_disable=1`, the SCST write cache is the cluster's coherence point, but P34D's fresh-source read used SCSI READ-FUA which pierces to the lagging platter — adopting an image older than the victim's own last flush, reverting its own just-created dirent. Fixed by sourcing the fresh dinode via plain (cache-coherent) read when `fua_disable=1`.

**Cluster state:** a stale SCSI persistent reservation (un-clearable from initiators, SCST PR state desynced) wedged the LUN before the verification run. Recovery is mid-flight: all 16 VMs destroyed, SCST restart on clyde was deactivating at handoff. Next session: confirm SCST active, `scripts/cluster_reset_n.sh 16` + `tests/reset4.sh 16`, confirm `863173A4` everywhere, then run the cluster-phase timing probe expecting no 120s timeouts, and finally the full criterion under 600s.

